+# Skibidi single-core performance results
+
+All reportable measurements materialize complete output bytes and retain API,
+RNG, probability, ABI, buffer, newline, `lengths`, and `call_count` semantics.
+Throughput conclusions use medians, never best-of-N.
+
+## 2026-08-05: trustworthy starting baseline
+
+### Snapshot and hypothesis
+
+- Decision: baseline only; no generator optimization in this round.
+- Git HEAD: `92143bd3f1388affa5adb5e899ff7a6e05c03ee5` with the user's
+  pre-existing correctness changes left uncommitted.
+- `skibidi_avx.c` SHA-256:
+  `48BD978AD4509A2EDB56E2FA58203F18E1EF9D0E8DB758FA960EF95C2F22B5BE`.
+- `skibidi_avx.h` SHA-256:
+  `BDE8E9D19D6668C644ABA1CDD81FB9F56C2236FF827DDD16FB366369BC68BBEA`.
+- Purpose: replace the ignored legacy best-of-N benchmark with a tracked,
+  checksummed, nine-run baseline before evaluating any optimization.
+
+### Environment
+
+- CPU: Intel Core Ultra 9 275HX; Windows CPU-set logical processor 10 has
+  `EfficiencyClass=1` (one of eight P-core-class logical processors).
+- Affinity: every process requested and observed WSL vCPU 10. Hyper-V does not
+  expose CPUID leaf `0x1a` core type, so Windows logical CPU 10 to WSL vCPU 10
+  is an explicitly recorded numbering assumption.
+- OS: WSL2, Linux `6.6.87.2-microsoft-standard-WSL2`, x86-64.
+- Compiler: GCC 13.3.0.
+- AVX2 flags: `-O3 -std=gnu11 -Wall -Wextra -Werror
+  -fno-omit-frame-pointer -march=native -mavx2`.
+- Scalar flags: `-O3 -std=gnu11 -Wall -Wextra -Werror
+  -fno-omit-frame-pointer -mno-avx -mno-avx2`.
+- Windows actual-frequency telemetry during AVX2: 30 samples, min 4938.87
+  MHz, median 5081.43 MHz, max 5136.21 MHz. `% Performance Limit` remained
+  100 and `Performance Limit Flags` remained 0.
+- Scalar telemetry: 18 samples, min 4748.79 MHz, median 5069.26 MHz, max
+  5123.95 MHz; limit flags remained 0.
+- WSL exposes neither cpufreq nor thermal sysfs. ACPI temperature is
+  unavailable. Kernel-log review found thermal-governor registration only,
+  not a throttling event. Temperature therefore cannot be claimed.
+- `perf` and `llvm-mca` are installed, but `perf_event_open` returns `ENOENT`
+  for hardware PMU events in this WSL VM. Actual core cycles, instructions,
+  branches, branch misses, and cache misses are reported as unavailable, not
+  substituted with TSC. Serialized invariant TSC runs at about 3.072 GHz and
+  is reported only as reference cycles.
+
+### Commands
+
+```powershell
+./benchmarks/windows-cpu-topology.ps1 | Format-Table -AutoSize
+wsl bash tests/run-tests.sh
+./benchmarks/run-reportable.ps1 -Mode avx2 -Cpu 10 -DurationMs 1000 `
+  -DramMiB 256 -OutputBase './benchmarks/results/2026-08-05-baseline-gcc-avx2-cpu10'
+./benchmarks/run-reportable.ps1 -Mode scalar -Cpu 10 -DurationMs 1000 `
+  -DramMiB 256 -OutputBase './benchmarks/results/2026-08-05-baseline-gcc-scalar-cpu10'
+```
+
+The correctness gate passed both `-march=native -mavx2` and
+`-mno-avx -mno-avx2` builds before measurement.
+
+### Results
+
+| Case | Throughput median | P5 | P95 | Latency median | Latency P95 | TSC ref cycles/op | Effective GB/s |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
+| AVX2 batch L1, 24 KiB | 112.011 M/s | 110.229 M/s | 112.259 M/s | 8.9277 ns | 9.0728 ns | 27.4259 | 3.1055 |
+| AVX2 batch L2, 255 KiB | 111.587 M/s | 111.002 M/s | 112.740 M/s | 8.9616 ns | 9.0089 ns | 27.5300 | 3.0938 |
+| AVX2 batch DRAM, 256 MiB | 110.546 M/s | 109.940 M/s | 111.197 M/s | 9.0460 ns | 9.0959 ns | 27.7893 | 3.0649 |
+| Scalar build generate L1 | 106.112 M/s | 104.747 M/s | 107.011 M/s | 9.4240 ns | 9.5476 ns | 28.9505 | 2.8360 |
+| Scalar build variant L1 | 102.601 M/s | 98.923 M/s | 102.996 M/s | 9.7465 ns | 10.1155 ns | 29.9411 | 2.6588 |
+
+Raw output and host telemetry are in:
+
+- `benchmarks/results/2026-08-05-baseline-gcc-avx2-cpu10.txt`
+- `benchmarks/results/2026-08-05-baseline-gcc-avx2-cpu10-windows-telemetry.csv`
+- `benchmarks/results/2026-08-05-baseline-gcc-scalar-cpu10.txt`
