+| Exact two-advance AVX2 RNG | 1.6198 G/s | 1.5093 / 1.6343 G/s | 0.6174 / 0.6646 ns | 1.8966 | n/a |
+| 32-byte record + newline + length stores | 3.6098 G/s | 3.5807 / 3.6484 G/s | 0.2770 / 0.2793 ns | 0.8510 | 133.5623 |
+
+Control telemetry captured 19 actual-frequency samples: 4927.64 MHz minimum,
+5051.26 MHz median, and 5093.59 MHz maximum, with performance limit 100% and
+flags 0. Disassembly proves the RNG control retains 16 pairs of four-lane
+xoroshiro128++ advances per 64 operations plus final RNG/accumulator stores.
+The store control retains 64 `vmovdqu` record stores, 64 newline stores, and
+all length stores per batch. These are real component ceilings, not tape or
+checksum-only generator claims.
