+
+## Final reportable results
+
+```powershell
+./benchmarks/run-reportable.ps1 -Mode avx2 -Compiler gcc -Cpu 10 `
+  -DurationMs 1000 -DramMiB 256 -OutputBase `
+  './benchmarks/results/2026-08-05-final-h09-gcc-avx2-cpu10'
+./benchmarks/run-reportable.ps1 -Mode scalar -Compiler gcc -Cpu 10 `
+  -DurationMs 1000 -DramMiB 256 -OutputBase `
+  './benchmarks/results/2026-08-05-final-h09-repeat-gcc-scalar-cpu10'
+```
+
+| Case | Final median | P5 / P95 | Latency median / P95 | TSC ref cycles/op | GB/s | Baseline multiple |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
+| AVX2 batch L1 | 181.680 M/s | 161.514 / 183.169 M/s | 5.5042 / 6.2091 ns | 16.9088 | 5.0371 | 1.6220x |
+| AVX2 batch L2 | 181.298 M/s | 171.194 / 182.303 M/s | 5.5158 / 5.8497 ns | 16.9444 | 5.0265 | 1.6247x |
+| AVX2 batch DRAM | 180.789 M/s | 180.000 / 181.932 M/s | 5.5313 / 5.5555 ns | 16.9922 | 5.0124 | 1.6354x |
+| Scalar generate L1 | 109.322 M/s | 82.142 / 111.917 M/s | 9.1473 / 12.4549 ns | 28.1004 | 2.9218 | 1.0303x |
+| Scalar variant L1 | 104.584 M/s | 91.168 / 105.467 M/s | 9.5617 / 10.9709 ns | 29.3732 | 2.7102 | 1.0193x |
+
+The AVX2 run sampled 5042.89 MHz median actual frequency (3481.56 minimum,
+5115.54 maximum), performance limit 100%, and flags 0. The scalar repeat was
+more externally disturbed (4671.95 MHz telemetry median and 2272.45 minimum),
+which explains its wide P5; its median and P95 still exceed the initial scalar
+baseline. Temperature remains unavailable and is not claimed.
