+## Retained and failed hypotheses
+
+Retained generator changes:
+
+- H02 fused raw-draw dop/dom oracle;
+- H03 complete four-record materialization unroll;
+- H05 ending-pair lookup tables;
+- H06 fallthrough rare-dop materialization;
+- H08 batch dop-count oracle;
+- H09 fused branchless approval/rejection ending table.
+
+Rejected or reverted changes:
+
+- H01 fixed 44-byte templates;
+- H04 outer-loop annotation and Clang 18 comparison;
+- H07 speculative branchless prophecy materialization;
+- H10 speculative second-dop store;
+- H11 scalar per-lane prophecy classification;
+- H12 GCC PGO;
+- H13 frame-pointer omission;
+- H14 one-store prefix table.
+
+This is 14 distinct profile/disassembly-backed hypotheses. H10 through H14 are
+five consecutive valid hypotheses with no reproducible >=1% reportable median
+gain, satisfying the fallback search condition after the last retained H09.
+
+## Measured upper-bound model and remaining gap
+
+The final L1 result is 18.17% of the 1.0 G/s formal target, a 5.50x gap. It is
+57.0x below the idealized 10.36 G/s 64-byte/cycle store-fabric reference, but
+that theoretical number excludes every required RNG, branch, lookup, offset,
+length, and compact-output dependency. The measured store control is the more
+relevant ceiling and is 19.87x faster than full generation.
+
+At the final AVX2 telemetry median, full generation is approximately 27.8
+frequency-normalized core cycles/op. Component-control telemetry gives about
+3.12 cycles/op for the exact RNG arithmetic and 1.40 cycles/op for the real
+record/newline/length stores. The same budget is visible without frequency
+normalization: 1.8966 + 0.8510 = 2.7476 serialized TSC reference cycles/op.
+At 1.0 G/s the approximately 3.072 GHz invariant TSC permits only 3.072
+reference cycles/op, leaving about 0.324 reference cycles/op for all entropy
+classification, random control flow, table loads, variable-length compaction,
+and API accounting. The frequency-normalized version leaves about 0.53 core
+cycles/op. Adding component controls is an optimistic budgeting model, not a
+claim that all execution ports serialize, but entropy must precede indexed
+materialization, so the original 3-5 total-cycle estimate is not supported by
+the measured component floors.
+
+Final disassembly contains 2,411 lines in `skibidi_generate_batch` and retains
+both vector RNG state stores, `vmovmskpd` prophecy classification, all output,
+newline, and length stores, fused `BATCH_DOP_ORACLE` and `BATCH_ENDINGS` loads,
+and compact-offset updates. Near-identical L1/L2/DRAM medians plus only
+5.04 GB/s full-generation bandwidth, versus 133.56 GB/s in the store control,
+rule out cache capacity and store ports as the active limit. The remaining
+bottleneck is the serial variable-length materialization graph: each next
+output address depends on the previous random length, while random prophecy
+branches and entropy-dependent table loads feed one-to-five dop stores.
+
+A materially higher result now requires a different architecture, not another
+local instruction substitution: classify a wider block, calculate vector
+prefix sums, materialize independently, and compact exact records while still
+preserving output order, every byte store, RNG sequence, and buffer boundary.
+The failed fixed-template and speculative-materialization rounds show that such
+a redesign must remove enough serial control work to repay its extra staging
+and copies. On the required evidence and stopping rule, 180-182 M/s is the
+reproducible ceiling of the current compact serial materializer on this WSL
+platform; the 1.0 G/s target is not supported without that architectural
+replacement.
